Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

EXT. PARK BENCH - AFTERNOON

Zoe and Jackie watch a dog trying to drag a stick through a fence. Claire is nearby, outside their conversation.

JACKIE
Do you forgive them?

ZOE
I don't know.

Jackie accepts that answer. The dog abandons the stick, chases something else.

JACKIE
Getting away should have felt bigger.

ZOE
Maybe that's not the ending.

Jackie waits.

ZOE
Agency.

JACKIE
Homework.

ZOE
Choice.

JACKIE
Say choice then.

They watch the dog return empty-mouthed. Neither girl needs a final verdict today.

INT. ELIAS'S ROOM - EVENING

His bag is partly packed. Zoe stands in the doorway. He talks about distance, protecting her by leaving.

ZOE
If you want to go, say that. Don't decide what I want and call it protection.

He sits. She takes the chair opposite. He can still choose to leave; she has not ordered him to stay.

ELIAS
I don't know how to stay without being responsible for everything.

ZOE
Then don't be responsible for everything.

ELIAS
You're thirteen. There'll be danger. Times I know more.

ZOE
You say move now. I move. Afterward, you explain. The rest we work out.

He takes time before answering her actual question.

ELIAS
I don't want to leave.

ZOE
Then unpack.

ELIAS
Bossy.

ZOE
Agency.

He laughs. Unpacks two shirts. Not everything. Enough for now.

INT. BREAKFAST ROOM - SATURDAY MORNING

A message from Ruth: next hearing, another reference for review, nothing Zoe must do today. She turns off the phone.

Into the backpack: water, crisps, fantasy book, phone. No folder. No drive.

ELIAS
Walk?

ZOE
Why?

ELIAS
Because.

Suspicious. Acceptable. She picks up the bag.

EXT. PATH JUNCTION - SATURDAY

After nearly a mile beside a hedge, the path divides. Left climbs towards the ridge. Right drops towards a river.

Elias stops with Zoe.

ELIAS
Which way?

ZOE
What do you think?

ELIAS
River. Less uphill.

ZOE
Strong argument. I want the view.

ELIAS
Then ridge.

ZOE
You said river.

ELIAS
You asked what I thought. Now you decide.

ZOE
No. We decide.

He looks at both paths again.

ELIAS
Ridge first. River on the way back.

She considers the proposal.

ZOE
Acceptable.

They turn left together. The backpack hangs loose from one shoulder.
